# AMD64 thunk export spec -- msimg32.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-15 second-game pass: DOOM's Vulkan build imports these and
# every one reported c000007b -- the loader found the native ppc64 module and
# correctly refused to splice it into a guest call, because no guest thunk
# existed.  Same class of gap as the first game, same one-line fix, which is
# the point: nothing here is per-title.
#
# vulkan-1 is the one that matters for that binary.  It renders through
# vulkan-1 -> winevulkan -> RADV with no D3D anywhere in the path, so this is
# the shortest route from a real game's draw calls to this machine's GPU.
DLL msimg32.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# ---------------------------------------- the ceiling, measured 2026-08-17
# This module is five exports and it emits two: GradientFill and
# TransparentBlt, both declared in wingdi.h, which the global probe already
# has.  The other three are refused and each for its own honest reason, so
# they are written down rather than left as a number:
#
#   AlphaBlend      "argument 10 (BLENDFUNCTION) is not integer/pointer class"
#       The one that matters, and the one this module exists for.  A
#       BLENDFUNCTION is { BYTE BlendOp; BYTE BlendFlags; BYTE SourceConstant-
#       Alpha; BYTE AlphaFormat; } -- FOUR BYTES, passed BY VALUE, and the
#       thunk descriptor this port publishes describes integer and pointer
#       slots only.
#
#       This one is CLOSEABLE and the route is worth recording, because the
#       .spec already models it correctly: msimg32.spec says
#       `AlphaBlend(long long long long long long long long long long long)`
#       -- eleven integer classes, the tenth of which IS the BLENDFUNCTION.
#       Both ABIs agree with that reading: MS-x64 passes a 4-byte aggregate in
#       the low half of the argument register, and ppc64le ELFv2 passes it
#       right-justified in a GPR, so the same 32 bits arrive in the same place.
#       What blocks it is only that the ORACLE reads wingdi.h, where the type
#       is spelled as a struct.  The fix is the dxvk_flat_surface.h pattern --
#       a PROBE-EXTRA header declaring this one export with a DWORD in that
#       position -- and it is deliberately NOT taken here, because asserting an
#       ABI equivalence in a header is exactly the kind of claim that needs a
#       value-checked gate behind it and this pass has not built one.  A guest
#       that calls AlphaBlend today binds a named sentinel and dies naming the
#       symbol; it does not blend the wrong pixels.
#
#   vSetDdrawflag   "no declaration found in Wine headers"
#       Ordinal 1, no arguments, and undocumented on Windows too.  Wine's
#       implementation is a no-op.
#
#   DllInitialize   "no declaration found in Wine headers"
#       A loader entry point, not an API; a guest never imports it.
#
# NO CALLBACK AND NO INTERFACE CROSSES THIS BOUNDARY: all three real exports
# forward straight into gdi32 (GdiAlphaBlend, GdiGradientFill,
# GdiTransparentBlt) and take handles, rectangles and a vertex array.
